"""
Four-wheel planar car: a rigid chassis on four slip wheels, the front pair steered through
a column and an Ackermann linkage, with quasi-static wheel loads, its road load, and ideal
sensors that send everything measured about the car on `bus`.

The chassis is a planar body of mass `m` and yaw inertia `Iz` at the center of mass, with the
front axle `a` ahead and the rear axle `b` behind it and the wheels `tw/2` to either side. The
steering wheel turns the column, which turns the linkage's input by `1/i_s` of its angle; the
linkage turns the front wheels on revolute joints. `QuasiStaticLoads` pushes each wheel's normal
load onto its tire, every `Wheel` reads its grip from the road `grip`, and `RoadLoad` puts the
drag, rolling resistance and along-slope weight of the mass `m` on the chassis. The sensors read
the chassis (`velocity`, `acceleration`, `position`, the last in the world frame), the steering
column (`steering_angle`) and each wheel (a `Sensors.WheelSlip` each), and the car's equations
put every reading on `bus`, with the sideslip angle beta = atan(vy / max(|vx|, 1 m/s)).

Ports:
- `steering` the steering-wheel shaft; its angle steers the car, positive to the left. It must
  be held or driven (a `Fixed`, or a position source): the wheels carry no aligning torque, so
  an open steering shaft leaves its angle undetermined.
- `chassis` the chassis frame at the center of mass, for a `RoadGrade` or a sensor of the model's
  own.
- `spin_fl`, `spin_fr`, `spin_rl`, `spin_rr` each wheel's shaft, where a brake or a drive
  attaches; open when nothing acts on the wheel. The car has no brakes: a model places a
  `Chassis.Wheel.BrakeActuator` or a `Chassis.Brakes.Caliper` on each shaft it brakes.
- `grade` the road gradient tan(alpha) along the heading, 0 on a flat road (or from a
  `RoadGrade` on `chassis`); `f_r` the rolling resistance coefficient (0.012 is a car tire on
  asphalt).
- `bus` everything measured about the car (`CarBus` lists the fields); read it with a `BusOut`.
  Other sensors a model places itself attach to `chassis`, `steering` and the `spin_*` shafts.

Assumptions: no suspension, so no roll, pitch or camber; the road load acts at the center of mass
along the heading (`RoadLoad`); gravity enters only through the wheel loads and the road load,
and the model must hold one planar `World` with `g = 0`, since the car lies in the road plane.
The car starts at rest at the world origin heading along x, with every wheel at rest; give
another start at the declaration,
`Car(body(v = initial [20.0, 0.0]), fl(inertia(w = initial 64.5)))`. Defaults are the course's
planar car (a mid-size sedan, assumed). The wheel frames must take no torque about the kingpin:
the steering column and linkage react on a fixed housing, so a steering reaction would go to the
ground, not the chassis.

Limit on Dyad 3.5.0: once the car yaws, the test harness's default code optimization gives
wrong results (JuliaComputing/DyadCompilerPasses.jl#43); straight-line runs are unaffected.
"""
component Car
  "Steering-wheel shaft"
  steering = Spline() {^steering}
  "Chassis frame at the center of mass"
  chassis = Frame2D() {^chassis}
  "Front-left wheel shaft"
  spin_fl = Spline() {^spin_fl}
  "Front-right wheel shaft"
  spin_fr = Spline() {^spin_fr}
  "Rear-left wheel shaft"
  spin_rl = Spline() {^spin_rl}
  "Rear-right wheel shaft"
  spin_rr = Spline() {^spin_rr}
  "Road gradient along the heading, tan(alpha)"
  grade = RealInput() {^grade}
  "Rolling resistance coefficient"
  f_r = RealInput() {^f_r}
  "Everything measured about the car"
  bus = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.CarBus() {^bus}
  "Road grip over world position, shared by the four wheels"
  structural parameter grip::VehicleComponents.Road.Grip = VehicleComponents.Road.grip("dyad://VehicleComponents/data/roads/uniform_mu.crg")
  "Vehicle mass"
  parameter m::Dyad.Mass = 1500.0
  "Yaw inertia"
  parameter Iz::MomentOfInertia = 2500.0
  "CG distance to the front axle"
  parameter a::Length = 1.2
  "CG distance to the rear axle"
  parameter b::Length = 1.5
  "Track width"
  parameter tw::Length = 1.55
  "Wheel rolling radius"
  parameter radius::Length = 0.31
  "One wheel's spin inertia"
  parameter J::MomentOfInertia = 1.0
  "Peak adhesion coefficient"
  parameter mu_A::Real = 1.0
  "Sliding friction coefficient"
  parameter mu_S::Real = 0.8
  "Front slip ratio at peak adhesion"
  parameter sAdhesion_f::Real = 0.12
  "Rear slip ratio at peak adhesion"
  parameter sAdhesion_r::Real = 0.09
  "Steering ratio, steering-wheel angle over road-wheel angle"
  parameter i_s::Real = 16.0
  "Kingpin track"
  parameter t_k::Length = tw
  "Ackermann fraction: 1 for full Ackermann, 0 for parallel steer"
  parameter ackermann::Real = 1.0
  "CG height above the road"
  parameter h_cg::Length = 0.0
  "Pass the chassis acceleration on to the wheel loads"
  structural parameter load_transfer::Boolean = false
  "Suspension lag of the load transfer"
  parameter T_lt::Time = 0.05
  body = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.Body(m = m, I = Iz, render = false, linearStatePriority = 2, r = initial [0.0, 0.0], v = initial [0.0, 0.0], phi = initial 0.0, w = initial 0.0) {^body}
  front = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.FixedTranslation(r = [a, 0.0], render = false) {^front}
  rear = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.FixedTranslation(r = [-b, 0.0], render = false) {^rear}
  arm_fl = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.FixedTranslation(r = [0.0, tw / 2], render = false) {^arm_fl}
  arm_fr = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.FixedTranslation(r = [0.0, -tw / 2], render = false) {^arm_fr}
  arm_rl = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.FixedTranslation(r = [0.0, tw / 2], render = false) {^arm_rl}
  arm_rr = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.FixedTranslation(r = [0.0, -tw / 2], render = false) {^arm_rr}
  kingpin_fl = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.Revolute(render = false) {^kingpin_fl}
  kingpin_fr = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.Revolute(render = false) {^kingpin_fr}
  column = RotationalComponents.Components.IdealGear(ratio = i_s) {^column}
  linkage = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.AckermannSteering(L = a + b, t_k = t_k, ackermann = ackermann) {^linkage}
  housing = RotationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^housing}
  loads = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.QuasiStaticLoads(m = m, a = a, b = b, tw = tw, h = h_cg, load_transfer = load_transfer, T_lt = T_lt) {^loads}
  fl = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.Wheel(grip = grip, radius = radius, J = J, mu_A = mu_A, mu_S = mu_S, sAdhesion = sAdhesion_f) {^fl}
  fr = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.Wheel(grip = grip, radius = radius, J = J, mu_A = mu_A, mu_S = mu_S, sAdhesion = sAdhesion_f) {^fr}
  rl = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.Wheel(grip = grip, radius = radius, J = J, mu_A = mu_A, mu_S = mu_S, sAdhesion = sAdhesion_r) {^rl}
  rr = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.Wheel(grip = grip, radius = radius, J = J, mu_A = mu_A, mu_S = mu_S, sAdhesion = sAdhesion_r) {^rr}
  roadload = VehicleComponents.Body.Planar.RoadLoad(m = m) {^roadload}
  velocity = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.AbsoluteVelocity() {^velocity}
  acceleration = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.AbsoluteAcceleration() {^acceleration}
  position = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.AbsolutePosition(resolve_in_frame = MultibodyComponents.ResolveInFrame.World()) {^position}
  steering_angle = RotationalComponents.Sensors.AngleSensor() {^steering_angle}
  slip_fl = VehicleComponents.Sensors.WheelSlip(radius = radius) {^slip_fl}
  slip_fr = VehicleComponents.Sensors.WheelSlip(radius = radius) {^slip_fr}
  slip_rl = VehicleComponents.Sensors.WheelSlip(radius = radius) {^slip_rl}
  slip_rr = VehicleComponents.Sensors.WheelSlip(radius = radius) {^slip_rr}
relations
  connect(body.frame_a, front.frame_a, rear.frame_a, loads.chassis, chassis, roadload.chassis, velocity.frame_a, acceleration.frame_a, position.frame_a) {^w1}
  connect(front.frame_b, arm_fl.frame_a, arm_fr.frame_a) {^w2}
  connect(rear.frame_b, arm_rl.frame_a, arm_rr.frame_a) {^w3}
  connect(arm_fl.frame_b, kingpin_fl.frame_a) {^w4}
  connect(kingpin_fl.frame_b, fl.frame_a, slip_fl.frame_a) {^w5}
  connect(arm_fr.frame_b, kingpin_fr.frame_a) {^w6}
  connect(kingpin_fr.frame_b, fr.frame_a, slip_fr.frame_a) {^w7}
  connect(arm_rl.frame_b, rl.frame_a, slip_rl.frame_a) {^w8}
  connect(arm_rr.frame_b, rr.frame_a, slip_rr.frame_a) {^w9}
  connect(steering, column.spline_a, steering_angle.spline) {^w10}
  connect(column.spline_b, linkage.spline_in) {^w11}
  connect(linkage.spline_left, kingpin_fl.flange_a) {^w12}
  connect(linkage.spline_right, kingpin_fr.flange_a) {^w13}
  connect(column.support, linkage.support, housing.spline) {^w14}
  connect(loads.fl, fl.load) {^w15}
  connect(loads.fr, fr.load) {^w16}
  connect(loads.rl, rl.load) {^w17}
  connect(loads.rr, rr.load) {^w18}
  connect(fl.spin, spin_fl, slip_fl.spline) {^w19}
  connect(fr.spin, spin_fr, slip_fr.spline) {^w20}
  connect(rl.spin, spin_rl, slip_rl.spline) {^w21}
  connect(rr.spin, spin_rr, slip_rr.spline) {^w22}
  connect(f_r, roadload.f_r) {^w27}
  connect(grade, roadload.grade) {^w28}
  bus.vx = velocity.v_x
  bus.vy = velocity.v_y
  bus.r = velocity.w
  bus.ax = acceleration.a_x
  bus.ay = acceleration.a_y
  bus.x = position.x
  bus.y = position.y
  bus.psi = position.phi
  bus.beta = atan(bus.vy / max(abs(bus.vx), 1.0))
  bus.delta_sw = steering_angle.phi
  bus.kappa_fl = slip_fl.kappa
  bus.kappa_fr = slip_fr.kappa
  bus.kappa_rl = slip_rl.kappa
  bus.kappa_rr = slip_rr.kappa
  bus.alpha_fl = slip_fl.alpha
  bus.alpha_fr = slip_fr.alpha
  bus.alpha_rl = slip_rl.alpha
  bus.alpha_rr = slip_rr.alpha
  bus.omega_fl = slip_fl.omega
  bus.omega_fr = slip_fr.omega
  bus.omega_rl = slip_rl.omega
  bus.omega_rr = slip_rr.omega
metadata {
